WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.900
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, amen.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:14.080
The reading from the Sinaxadion, for July 9th, on which we commemorate the Holy Hyromarter

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.300
Pancratios.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:22.780
On the 9th of the month, we celebrate the memory of the Holy Hyromarter Pancratios, Bishop

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.220
of Tarmina.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:33.100
Saint Pancratios was born in Antioch during the time of the earthly sojourn of our Lord Jesus

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:34.320
Christ.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:40.680
His parents, having heard the Lord's miracles and teaching extoled, went with their young son

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.060
to Jerusalem and were baptized.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:49.580
After their deaths, Pancratios renounced all that bound him to this transitory world and

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:56.700
went to the shore of the black sea, where he practiced askecies in a cave in order to

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.940
be aware of nothing but himself and God.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:07.580
The Holy Apostle Peter, passing through the area to proclaim the gospel, encountered

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:13.740
the young ascetic and persuaded him to go with him on his travels.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:20.080
Going to Antioch, Pancratios was consecrated bishop for the town of Tarmina in Sicily,

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:26.260
along with Marcian, another of the Apostles' disciples, who had come from Jerusalem and

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:30.340
who was ordained for Syracuse.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:38.760
During sale for Sicily, Saint Pancratios converted the whole crew and also the captain, Lyconidas.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:45.720
They arrived in Sicily after a pleasant voyage, and when the saints set foot on the shore,

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:51.220
the demons that were in an idol of the God Falcon, to which the people had to offer human

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:56.840
sacrifice every year, began to scream with terror.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:03.400
The saint invoked the name of the Holy Trinity, raising as a staff the cross he was carrying

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:09.440
in his hand, and the demons immediately threw the statue into the sea.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:15.920
Lyconidas, having recounted the miracles worked by Christ and his servants to Boniface, the

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:22.720
governor of the city, the latter summoned the bishop, but Pancratios asked that the governor

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:25.320
come to him.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:31.680
Lyconidas fell on his face to the earth when he saw the glory surrounding the saint, and

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.280
he came to believe in Christ on hearing his preaching.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:42.220
After having been instructed, along with his retinue throughout the night, the governor asked

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:45.720
Pancratios to go and bless his palace.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:52.840
He was received with great honor and stayed for forty days, obtaining Boniface's authorization

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:59.780
to build a church in the city, the limits of which he traced himself.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:05.600
The building was quickly finished, and at its consecration, all those present could see

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:12.860
an awe-inspiring fire descending and illuminating the entire church, and before the saint had

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:19.960
finished celebrating the divine liturgy, all the idols in the city were destroyed.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:25.560
The pagan priests went yelling to the palace and reproached the governor for keeping feast

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:29.400
when such a catastrophe had struck the city.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:35.960
Boniface succeeded in containing their agitation, and asked what the most learned among them

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:41.600
thought to be the reason for the idols falling to pieces.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:48.560
Maybe some other more powerful God had appeared and cast them down.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:54.840
Through the imprecations of one of the pagan priests, a demon called Lisan replied that

00:03:54.840 --> 00:04:02.520
the God in three persons had rendered them powerless by the incarnation of the sun, him whom

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:10.840
the stranger brought by Lycanides had come and preached in the city of Taormina.

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:18.340
The idolaters remaining unmoved by this confession decided to sacrifice the governor himself as

00:04:18.340 --> 00:04:22.100
a sign of expiation.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:29.500
Saint Pancratios, warned by a terrified Boniface, spent the whole night in prayer in the church.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:35.860
In the morning, they were preparing to emulate Boniface when Pancratios appeared, clothed in

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:40.780
his episcopal vestments, across in hand.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:46.860
Boniface's bonds were loosed at once, and all the pagans present fell to the ground before

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:51.540
the radiance that emanated from the holy prelate.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:57.700
Pancratios ordered the idol of Lisan to go and throw itself into the sea, and he killed

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:03.620
an enormous serpent that was feeding on the blood of the victims.

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:09.500
All then cried out, great is the God of Pancratios.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:15.380
The great number of them were baptized, and the people who lived on the slopes of Etna

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:21.460
imitated them when they saw the healings accomplished by the saint.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:27.740
A temple priestess, suffering from leprosy, was healed by the saint.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:34.660
But when she uttered blasphemies, she was once again struck by this disease in a more serious

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:36.140
form.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:44.140
Repenting, she received baptism under the name of Benedicta, and, after having been ordained

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:51.140
deaconess, went and broke up with her own hands, the idols that she had formerly served,

00:05:51.140 --> 00:05:54.660
giving the gold to the poor.

00:05:54.660 --> 00:06:00.700
As Boniface had to leave on a campaign with a vast army, he had his men blessed by the

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:06.340
saint, and a great many of the soldiers, on beholding the divine glory that surrounded

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:10.940
him, asked to receive baptism.

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:16.780
A cloud from heaven covered the saint during the liturgy that he then celebrated before

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:24.140
them, and a disappeared at the moment of the elevation of the holy gifts.

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:31.500
Boniface had left a certain alethas to replace him in the city, a callus and debauched pagan

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:37.140
who coveted one of the virgins consecrated to God by the saint.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:44.020
After the mediation of a disciple of mountainous, he cast a spell on the young virgin, but

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:46.900
it was ineffective.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:54.620
He then had the virgins arrested, and they, remaining inflexible under the pagan's pressure,

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:58.040
were beheaded.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:04.720
St. Pancratios buried them in the presence of the people, and built a church in their honor.

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:11.680
As soon as Boniface returned to Tormina, he had elitist, punished, and encouraged the

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:20.200
building of churches all over Sicily, where disciples of St. Pancratios made many conversions.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:28.440
Achilinos, king of Calabria, having besieged Tormina at the head of a powerful army, Pancratios

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:36.000
urged the people to place their hope in Christ, and even sent home the men who were manning

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.440
the ramparts.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:46.040
He then climbed a promontory, armed with a cross and two icons, and blessed the city in

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:49.200
all four directions.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:57.360
The enemy, seeing as it seemed three brilliant sons, fled, killing one another.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:04.080
Some of them, however, gave themselves up, and, after having baptized them, the saint

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:10.410
sent them to Calabria to preach the good news.

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:17.890
During a new campaign of Bonifaces, his replacement Artagoras invited the bishop to a banquet,

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:23.330
in the course of which the saint threw down an idol that had been placed there.

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:27.210
The pagans then launched themselves on him.

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:34.250
He threw him to the ground, and beat him so violently that he gave up the ghost.

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:40.450
They then threw his body into a crevasse, where he was found by the faithful after anxious

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.290
searching.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:48.610
Bonifaces, on his return from the war, punished those guilty, and had a golden sarcophagus

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:53.010
made to receive the body of the holy prelet.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:59.670
Its saint Pancratios appeared to his disciple and successor Evagrius, to ask him to bury

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:05.170
in the bare earth him who had always despised gold.

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:12.890
During the funeral, his body appeared free of any wound and radiant with glory, and a delightful

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:16.370
fragrance spread around it.

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:24.170
A church was then built in honor of Saint Pancratios, disciple of the apostles and protector

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:26.690
of the city.

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:33.450
Through the prayers of our holy fathers, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:34.450
and save us.
